    "body": "## Current Review Note\nPR 22 surfaced a loading-state preference that should stay out of the token-card PR: loading affordances should be local to the affected card/section, not a full-screen or page-wide sweep.\n\n## Clarified Loading Direction\n- Cards: if cards reload, loading should be clipped inside each card.\n- Chart: should have a chart-local loading state/skeleton instead of only a text note or blank redraw.\n- Tables: model/history tables should use table-local loading rows/states.\n- No full-page shimmer/sweep unless the whole page is intentionally blocked.\n\n## Out of Scope\nThis issue should standardize UX states. Actual endpoint latency/performance optimization should be tracked separately so it can include timing, SQL/query profiling, caching, and API aggregation changes.\n",
